{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>First interpretation</b><br>במסבו — like ומסבי ירושלם — an expensive round structure." "My nard — a spice resembling saffron." "<b>Second interpretation</b><br>She answered: Even though I have a good fragrance, for the king too, [when he is at his banqueting house], desired to smell my nard — [there is] to you [a still better good fragrance: the bundle of myrrh], and I desired that he lodge between my breasts and embrace the one resembling a cluster of henna from the village that is at En Gedi." "<b>Third interpretation</b><br>She said — the Congregation of Israel: Remember for me the covenant of Abraham, whose fame went out in all the world like nard, and was placed in the bundle of myrrh."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:54.513028261Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}